{"id":"evt_x4rxznyg","issue_id":"fxl-trzm","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-05-30T18:00:21.128941Z","changes":[{"field":"title","from":"Extract reusable STT TTS and LLM service clients from kitt","to":"Integrate Codec with Pi overlay RPC events"},{"field":"description","from":"Adapt the useful WebSocket STT/TTS clients and OpenAI-compatible LLM wrapper from ../kitt into codec-specific services. Keep browser-first boundaries and avoid copying the Tauri-heavy App.tsx lifecycle.","to":"Build the Codec-side client for the Pi runtime overlay protocol instead of owning STT, TTS, and LLM directly. Consume session state, transcript, assistant text, active contact, and audio-level events from Pi; send overlay commands such as submit text, interrupt, mute, and contact activation."}]}
{"id":"evt_5dwvddsa","issue_id":"fxl-mk5x","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-05-30T18:00:25.874400Z","changes":[{"field":"description","from":"Create the data model for codec contacts such as Colonel, including id, display name, frequency, portrait asset, system prompt, TTS voice, speed, and optional LLM model override.","to":"Create the data model for Codec contacts such as Colonel, including id, display name, frequency, portrait asset, Pi contact id, optional Pi session id, voice metadata, and display hints. Contact activation should be declarative: Codec sends contacts.activate and Pi decides whether that means persona switch, session switch, or runtime profile switch."}]}
{"id":"evt_f1vywtcg","issue_id":"fxl-624s","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-05-30T18:00:31.865620Z","changes":[{"field":"description","from":"Provide initial browser-first configuration for STT WebSocket URL, TTS WebSocket URL, LLM base URL/model, VAD timeout, default contact, and contact profiles. Leave a path to migrate to XDG config.toml if this becomes a Tauri desktop app.","to":"Provide initial browser-first Codec overlay configuration: Pi RPC/WebSocket URL, default contact/frequency, contact display profiles, reconnect behavior, and UI defaults. Do not configure STT/TTS/LLM providers here; those belong to the Pi runtime/extension side so KITT and Codec share the same voice/session pipeline."}]}
{"id":"evt_786azjyb","issue_id":"fxl-jjh0","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-05-30T18:00:36.095460Z","changes":[{"field":"title","from":"Implement codec conversation state machine","to":"Implement Codec overlay state machine"},{"field":"description","from":"Centralize app state transitions for idle, connecting, listening, thinking, speaking, and error. Use this state machine to coordinate STT input, LLM generation, TTS playback, interruption, and UI animation.","to":"Centralize Codec overlay state transitions for disconnected, connecting, idle, listening, thinking, speaking, and error. Drive state from Pi runtime events rather than local STT/LLM/TTS ownership, while still supporting UI commands such as contact activation, interrupt, mute, and manual text submit."}]}
{"id":"evt_752pjm6v","issue_id":"fxl-c6y4","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-05-30T18:00:39.754637Z","changes":[{"field":"description","from":"Use microphone input volume and TTS output volume to animate codec signal bars, portrait activity, listening countdown, and speaking indicators. Start with the analyser patterns proven in ../kitt.","to":"Use audio-level and runtime-state events from the Pi overlay stream to animate Codec signal bars, portrait activity, listening countdown, and speaking indicators. Avoid direct microphone/TTS analyser ownership in Codec unless a later standalone mode explicitly needs it."}]}
{"id":"evt_scck6zex","issue_id":"fxl-nmpn","action":"updated","timestamp":"2026-05-30T18:00:44.243229Z","changes":[{"field":"title","from":"Build first end-to-end Colonel conversation","to":"Build first end-to-end Colonel overlay flow"},{"field":"description","from":"Connect the scaffolded UI, contact model, STT, LLM, and TTS into a first playable codec call with the Colonel profile. Include transcript display, interruption handling, and visible connection/error states.","to":"Connect the scaffolded Codec UI to a live Pi runtime via RPC/events for a first playable Colonel contact flow. Frequency/contact activation should call Pi RPC, Pi owns the session and voice pipeline, and Codec displays transcript, assistant response, speaking/listening state, interruption, and connection/error states."}]}
